# Version 2 · cold open on the whip lying on the floor, the story told as a flashback
title: Do Not Be Afraid
subtitle: Version 2 · The Flashback
tempo: 90
key: C minor
music: noir
intensity: 0.9
grade: ash
images: ../assets/img/{}-2.webp
endnote: "Here I am! I stand at the door and knock."
endref: Revelation 3:20

@0:00-0:02.5 black cue:drone,0.5
@0:02.5-0:09 img:whipfloor ken:slow
vo: It lay still on the stone.
vo: The tables overturned. The doves gone up into the light.
@0:09-0:13 img:tables ken:drift
title: What happened here?
@0:13-0:15 drop:"Greater love has no one than this" ref:"John 15:13"

# the flashback, in warm colour
@0:15-0:18 img:light ken:push fade grade:warm cue:wonder,0.8
sfx: spark
@0:18-0:24 img:child ken:up grade:warm
vo: Before anything was made, there was love.
@0:24-0:29 img:steps ken:down fx:flare grade:warm
vo: Not a little. Not enough.
+2 title: Overflowing
@0:29-0:35 img:turn ken:in grade:warm
vo: For the lost. For the misguided.
vo: For the ones who would wound Him.
@0:35-0:39 img:smile ken:still hold:silent grade:warm
@0:39-0:44 img:childcords ken:in grade:warm cue:wonder,1
vo: Nothing you do to the body can touch what He holds.
@0:44-0:50 img:kneel ken:in cue:tense,0.7
vo: "Whoever causes one of these little ones to stumble..."
ref: Matthew 18:6
@0:50-0:56 img:millstone ken:down
vo: "...better for them to have a millstone hung around their neck."
@0:56-1:02 img:door ken:push cue:tense,1
vo: "I never knew you."
ref: Matthew 7:23
@1:02-1:04 drop:"The truth will set you free" ref:"John 8:32"
@1:04-1:08 img:temple ken:right cue:build
text: Do not bargain with darkness.
@1:08-1:12 img:take ken:in
text: Overturn the tables / in your own heart.
@1:12-1:16 cuts:cords,knot,knot!,eyes,braid,whip cue:war
text: He made a whip of cords.
ref: John 2:15
@1:16-1:21 img:tables ken:slow hit:2 grade:warm
vo: "...and drove them all out of His Father's house."
@1:21-1:26 img:doves ken:up fx:flare cue:choir grade:warm
text: We do not fight people.
text: We fight for them.
# back to the present
@1:26-1:31 img:whipfloor ken:still cue:choir,0.6
vo: That is why it lay on the stone.
+2.5 title: Love is not weak.
@1:31-1:33 drop:"Take heart. I have overcome the world." ref:"John 16:33"
@1:33-1:40 img:weep ken:slow cue:weep
vo: He wept over the city,
vo: because it did not recognize the time of God's coming.
ref: Luke 19:41–44
@1:40-1:42 img:stone ken:push hit:2
@1:42-1:47 img:ruins ken:left
vo: "Not one stone will be left on another."
ref: Matthew 24:2 · 70 AD
@1:47-1:52 img:redsea ken:in cue:drone,0.8
sfx: braam
vo: "The Lord will fight for you."
ref: Exodus 14:14
@1:52-2:04 img:grown ken:in cue:heart
text: I will not fear.
text: Fear makes the soul small.
text: Let it come. / Let it pass through me.
text: Only He remains.
@2:04-2:11 img:stand ken:up fx:rise cue:tutti grade:warm
vo: "Do not fear, for I am with you."
ref: Isaiah 41:10
@2:11-2:14 img:dawn ken:push hit:2 grade:warm
title: So stand.
@2:14-2:19 img:opendoor ken:in fade cue:outro grade:warm
text: You were never forced.
text: You were invited.
@2:19-2:24 black
title: Do not be afraid.
